README-ARCHIVERS -- twenty programs, seven formats, and which to takeIf you are copying part of this collection onto your own media you want ONEarchiver, and probably a second to read something a friend sends you.  Thisfile is here so you do not have to install seven and try them.Short answer: take `tar' to pack your own things and `unzip' to open whatother people send.  `tar' is 22K, needs no Microware module, and its formatis the one every other system can still read; it is also what this disk wasbuilt with.  `unzip' reads the format the rest of the world settled on, andnothing here can WRITE one you would want to send (see `zip' below).THE TWENTY FILES ARE SEVEN FORMATS----------------------------------A star means the program needs Microware's `cio' -- which ships here, so itcosts you nothing on this disk, but it is one more file to carry if you aretaking a program away.  DOC/README-CIO explains.  format        write            read only        needs cio  -------------------------------------------------------------------  ARC           arc, marc        --               --  LHarc         lha, lharc       xlharc           --  zoo           zoo              booz, fiz        zoo, booz, fiz  tar           tar, gtar        --               --  zip           zip              unzip, zipinfo   unzip, zipinfo  compress      compress, compr  --               --  gzip          gzip             gzip             --  shell archive shar             sh               --  ar (library)  ar, ar2          --               ar2  file              bytes  cio  module     source  docs  --------------------------------------------------------------  tar               22966  no   tar        --      4 files  REBUILT/gtar     113562  no   gtar       yes     --  zip               63972  no   zip        --      1  unzip             42060  yes  unzip      --      6 files  zipinfo           23904  yes  zipinfo    --      1  lha               65560  no   LHa